{"issue": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2814", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2814/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2814/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2814/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2814", "id": 4161791365, "node_id": "I_kwDOBabE0s74D-WF", "number": 2814, "title": "Expose io_context for external event loop integration", "user": {"login": "bansiesta", "id": 10187973, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTg3OTcz", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10187973?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/bansiesta", "html_url": "https://github.com/bansiesta", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bansiesta/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bansiesta/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bansiesta/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bansiesta/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bansiesta/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bansiesta/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bansiesta/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bansiesta/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bansiesta/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 2, "created_at": "2026-03-28T21:58:10Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-28T23:05:23Z", "closed_at": "2026-03-28T23:05:23Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "COLLABORATOR", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "## Problem\n\nCurrently MAVSDK always owns its `asio::io_context` and runs it on an internal `_io_thread`. There is no way for an application that already runs its own Asio event loop (e.g. a drone autopilot written with Asio, or a ROS2 node using its own executor) to share the io_context with MAVSDK.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\nAdd a `Mavsdk` constructor overload that accepts an `asio::io_context&`:\n\n\\`\\`\\`cpp\nMavsdk(Configuration configuration, asio::io_context& external_io_context);\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nWhen constructed this way:\n- MAVSDK does not start `_io_thread`\n- The caller is responsible for calling `io_context.run()` (or integrating it into their event loop via `poll()` / `run_one()` etc.)\n- All other behaviour is identical\n\n## Design considerations\n\n- Exposing `asio::io_context` in `mavsdk.h` means Asio becomes part of the public API. We may need a forward-declared wrapper or an `any_io_executor` variant to keep the public header clean.\n- An alternative: expose a `run_once()` / `poll()` method that lets callers drive the event loop without exposing the type directly \u2014 but this is less idiomatic for Asio users.\n- Related: `set_callback_executor()` already lets users redirect _callbacks_ to their own thread. This issue is about integrating the _I/O loop_ itself.\n\n## Context\n\nThis came up after #2810 which migrated all internal I/O to a single Asio io_context. That PR is a prerequisite for this feature.", "closed_by": {"login": "bansiesta", "id": 10187973, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTg3OTcz", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10187973?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/bansiesta", "html_url": "https://github.com/bansiesta", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bansiesta/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bansiesta/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "htt